H3200.definition:
patronymically from H3199 (יָכִין)lemma יִכִין first vowel, corrected to יָכִין;
a Jakinite (collectively) or descendants of Jakin
KJV: Jachinites.

H3201.definition:
or (fuller) יָכוֹל; a primitive root;
to be able, literally (can, could) or morally (may, might)
KJV: be able, any at all (ways), attain, can (away with, (-not)), could, endure, might, overcome, have power, prevail, still, suffer.

H3202.definition:
(Aramaic) or יְכִיל; (Aramaic), to H3201 (יָכֹל)
{to be able, literally (can, could) or morally (may, might)}
KJV: be able, can, couldest, prevail.

H3203.definition:
and יְכׇלְיָהוּ; or (2 Chronicles 26:3) יְכִילְיָה; from H3201 (יָכֹל) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah will enable;
Jekoljah or Jekiljah, an Israelitess
KJV: Jecholiah, Jecoliah.

H3204.definition:
and יְכׇנְיָהוּ; or (Jeremiah 27:20) יְכוֹנְיָה; from H3559 (כּוּן) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah will establish;
Jekonjah, a Jewish king
KJV: Jeconiah. Compare H3659 (כׇּנְיָהוּ).

H3205.definition:
a primitive root;
to bear young; causatively, to beget; medically, to act as midwife; specifically, to show lineage
KJV: bear, beget, birth(-day), born, (make to) bring forth (children, young), bring up, calve, child, come, be delivered (of a child), time of delivery, gender, hatch, labour, (do the office of a) midwife, declare pedigrees, be the son of, (woman in, woman that) travail(-eth, -ing woman).

H3206.definition:
from H3205 (יָלַד);
something born, i.e. a lad or offspring
KJV: boy, child, fruit, son, young man (one).

H3207.definition:
feminine of H3206 (יֶלֶד);
a lass
KJV: damsel, girl.

H3208.definition:
abstractly from H3206 (יֶלֶד);
boyhood (or girlhood)
KJV: childhood, youth.

H3209.definition:
passive from H3205 (יָלַד);
born
KJV: born.

H3210.definition:
from H3885 (לוּן); lodging;
Jalon, an Israelite
KJV: Jalon.

H3211.definition:
from H3205 (יָלַד);
born
KJV: (home-) born, child, son.

H3212.definition:
a primitive root (compare H1980 (הָלַךְ));
to walk (literally or figuratively); causatively, to carry (in various senses)
KJV: [idiom] again, away, bear, bring, carry (away), come (away), depart, flow, [phrase] follow(-ing), get (away, hence, him), (cause to, made) go (away, -ing, -ne, one's way, out), grow, lead (forth), let down, march, prosper, [phrase] pursue, cause to run, spread, take away (-journey), vanish, (cause to) walk(-ing), wax, [idiom] be weak.

H3213.definition:
a primitive root;
to howl (with a wailing tone) or yell (with a boisterous one)
KJV: (make to) howl, be howling.

H3214.definition:
from H3213 (יָלַל);
a howl
KJV: howling.

H3215.definition:
feminine of H3214 (יְלֵל)
{a howl}
KJV: a howling.

H3216.definition:
a primitive root;
to blurt or utter inconsiderately
KJV: devour.

H3217.definition:
from an unused root apparently meaning to stick or scrape;
scurf or tetter
KJV: scabbed.

H3218.definition:
from an unused root meaning to lick up;
a devourer; specifically, the young locust
KJV: cankerworm, caterpillar.

H3219.definition:
from H3950 (לָקַט);
a travelling pouch (as if for gleanings)
KJV: scrip.

H3220.definition:
from an unused root meaning to roar;
a sea (as breaking in noisy surf) or large body of water; specifically (with the article), the Mediterranean Sea; sometimes a large river, or an artifical basin; locally, the west, or (rarely) the south
KJV: sea ([idiom] -faring man, (-shore)), south, west (-ern, side, -ward).

H3221.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3220 (יָם)
{a sea (as breaking in noisy surf) or large body of water; specifically (with the article), the Mediterranean Sea; sometimes a large river, or an artifical basin; locally, the west, or (rarely) the south}
KJV: sea.

H3222.definition:
from the same as H3117 (יוֹם);
a warm spring
KJV: mule.

H3223.definition:
from H3117 (יוֹם) and H410 (אֵל); day of God;
Jemuel, an Israelite
KJV: Jemuel.

H3224.definition:
perhaps from the same as H3117 (יוֹם); properly, warm, i.e. affectionate; hence, dove (compare H3123 (יוֹנָה));
Jemimah, one of Job's daughters
KJV: Jemimah.

H3225.definition:
from H3231 (יָמַן);
the right hand or side (leg, eye) of a person or other object (as the stronger and more dexterous); locally, the south
KJV: [phrase] left-handed, right (hand, side), south.

H3226.definition:
the same as H3225 (יָמִין);
Jamin, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Jamin. See also H1144 (בִּנְיָמִין).

H3227.definition:
for H3225 (יָמִין);
right
KJV: (on the) right (hand).

H3228.definition:
patronymically from H3226 (יָמִין);
a Jeminite (collectively) or descendants of Jamin
KJV: Jaminites. See also H1145 (בֶּן־יְמִינִי).

H3229.definition:
or יִמְלָה; from H4390 (מָלֵא); full;
Jimla or Jimlah, an Israelite
KJV: Imla, Imlah.

H3230.definition:
from H4427 (מָלַךְ); he will make king;
Jamlek, an Israelite
KJV: Jamlech.

H3232.definition:
from H3231 (יָמַן); prosperity (as betokened by the right hand);
Jimnah, the name of two Israelites; also (with the article) of the posterity of one of them
KJV: Imna, Imnah, Jimnah, Jimnites.

H3233.definition:
from H3231 (יָמַן);
right (i.e. at the right hand)
KJV: (on the) right (hand).

H3234.definition:
from H4513 (מָנַע); he will restrain;
Jimna, an Israelite
KJV: Imna.

H3235.definition:
a primitive root;
to exchange; by implication, to change places
KJV: boast selves, change.

H3236.definition:
probably from H3235 (יָמַר); interchange;
Jimrah, an Israelite
KJV: Imrah.

H3237.definition:
a primitive root;
to touch
KJV: feel.

H3238.definition:
a primitive root;
to rage or be violent; by implication, to suppress, to maltreat
KJV: destroy, (thrust out by) oppress(-ing, -ion, -or), proud, vex, do violence.

H3239.definition:
from H3240 (יָנַח); quiet;
Janoach or Janochah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Janoah, Janohah.

H3240.definition:
a primitive root;
to deposit; by implication, to allow to stay
KJV: bestow, cast down, lay (down, up), leave (off), let alone (remain), pacify, place, put, set (down), suffer, withdraw, withhold. (The Hiphil forms with the dagesh are here referred to, in accordance with the older grammarians; but if any distinction of the kind is to be made, these should rather be referred to H5117 (נוּחַ), and the others here.)

H3241.definition:
from H5123 (נוּם); asleep;
Janim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Janum (from the margin).

H3242.definition:
from H3243 (יָנַק);
a sucker or sapling
KJV: young twig.

H3243.definition:
a primitive root;
to suck; causatively, to give milk
KJV: milch, nurse(-ing mother), (give, make to) suck(-ing child, -ling).

H3245.definition:
a primitive root;
to set (literally or figuratively); intensively, to found; reflexively, to sit down together, i.e. settle, consult
KJV: appoint, take counsel, establish, (lay the, lay for a) found(-ation), instruct, lay, ordain, set, [idiom] sure.

H3246.definition:
from H3245 (יָסַד);
a foundation (figuratively, i.e. beginning)
KJV: [idiom] began.

H3247.definition:
from H3245 (יָסַד);
a foundation (literally or figuratively)
KJV: bottom, foundation, repairing

H3248.definition:
feminine of H3246 (יְסֻד);
a foundation
KJV: foundation.

H3249.definition:
from H5493 (סוּר);
departing
KJV: they that depart

H3250.definition:
from H3256 (יָסַר);
a reprover
KJV: instruct.

H3251.definition:
a primitive root;
to pour (intransitive)
KJV: be poured.

H3252.definition:
from an unused root meaning to watch; observant;
Jiskah, sister of Lot
KJV: Iscah.

H3253.definition:
from H5564 (סָמַךְ) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah will sustain;
Jismakjah, an Israelite
KJV: Ismachiah.

H3254.definition:
a primitive root;
to add or augment (often adverbial, to continue to do a thing)
KJV: add, [idiom] again, [idiom] any more, [idiom] cease, [idiom] come more, [phrase] conceive again, continue, exceed, [idiom] further, [idiom] gather together, get more, give more-over, [idiom] henceforth, increase (more and more), join, [idiom] longer (bring, do, make, much, put), [idiom] (the, much, yet) more (and more), proceed (further), prolong, put, be (strong-) er, [idiom] yet, yield.

H3255.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3254 (יָסַף)
{to add or augment (often adverbial, to continue to do a thing)}
KJV: add.

H3256.definition:
a primitive root;
to chastise, literally (with blows) or figuratively (with words); hence, to instruct
KJV: bind, chasten, chastise, correct, instruct, punish, reform, reprove, sore, teach.

H3257.definition:
from H3261 (יָעָה);
a shovel
KJV: shovel.

H3258.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to grieve; sorrowful;
Jabets, the name of an Israelite, and also of a place in Palestine
KJV: Jabez.

H3259.definition:
a primitive root;
to fix upon (by agreement or appointment); by implication, to meet (at a stated time), to summon (to trial), to direct (in a certain quarter or position), to engage (for marriage)
KJV: agree,(maxke an) appoint(-ment, a time), assemble (selves), betroth, gather (selves, together), meet (together), set (a time).

H3260.definition:
from H3259 (יָעַד); appointed;
Jedi, an Israelite
KJV: Iddo (from the margin) See H3035 (יִדּוֹ).

H3262.definition:
from H3261 (יָעָה) and H410 (אֵל); carried away of God;
Jeuel, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Jehiel, Jeiel, Jeuel. Compare H3273 (יְעִיאֵל).

H3263.definition:
from H5779 (עוּץ); counsellor;
Jeuts, an Israelite
KJV: Jeuz

H3264.definition:
a variation of H3298 (יַעֲרֶשְׁיָה);
a forest
KJV: wood.

H3265.definition:
apparently the passive participle of the same as H3293 (יַעַר); wooded;
Jaur, an Israelite
KJV: Jair(from the margin).

H3266.definition:
from H5789 (עוּשׁ); hasty;
Jeush, the name of an Edomite and of four Israelites
KJV: Jehush, Jeush. Compare H3274 (יְעִישׁ).

H3267.definition:
a primitive root;
to be bold or obstinate
KJV: fierce.

H3268.definition:
from H3267 (יָעַז) and H410 (אֵל); emboldened of God;
Jaaziel, an Israelite
KJV: Jaaziel.

H3269.definition:
from H3267 (יָעַז) and H3050 (יָהּ); emboldened of Jah;
Jaazijah, an Israelite
KJV: Jaaziah.

H3270.definition:
or יַעְזֵר; from H5826 (עָזַר); helpful;
Jaazer or Jazer, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Jaazer, Jazer.

H3271.definition:
a primitive root;
to clothe
KJV: cover.

H3272.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H3289 (יָעַץ);
to counsel; reflexively, to consult
KJV: counsellor, consult together.

H3273.definition:
from H3261 (יָעָה) and H410 (אֵל); carried away of God;
Jeiel, the name of six Israelites
KJV: Jeiel, Jehiel. Compare H3262 (יְעוּאֵל).

H3274.definition:
from H5789 (עוּשׁ); hasty;
Jeish, the name of an Edomite and of a an Israelite
KJV: Jeush (from the margin). Compare H3266 (יְעוּשׁ).

H3275.definition:
from the same as H5912 (עָכָן); troublesome;
Jakan, an Israelite
KJV: Jachan.

H3276.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to ascend; figuratively, to be valuable (objectively; useful, subjectively; benefited)
KJV: [idiom] at all, set forward, can do good, (be, have) profit, (able).

H3277.definition:
from H3276 (יַעַל);
an ibex (as climbing)
KJV: wild goat.

H3278.definition:
the same as H3277 (יָעֵל);
Jael, a Canaanite
KJV: Jael.

H3279.definition:
or יַעֲלָה; the same as H3280 (יַעֲלָה) or direct from H3276 (יַעַל);
Jaala or Jaalah, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Jaala, Jaalah.

H3280.definition:
feminine of H3277 (יָעֵל)
{an ibex (as climbing)}
KJV: roe.

H3281.definition:
from H5956 (עָלַם); occult;
Jalam, an Edomite
KJV: Jalam.

H3282.definition:
from an unused root meaning to pay attention;
properly, heed; by implication, purpose (sake or account); used adverbially to indicate the reason or cause
KJV: because (that), forasmuch ([phrase] as), seeing then, [phrase] that, [phrase] wheras, [phrase] why.

H3283.definition:
from the same as H3282 (יַעַן);
the ostrich (probably from its answering cry
KJV: ostrich.

H3284.definition:
feminine of H3283 (יָעֵן), and meaning the same
{the ostrich (probably from its answering cry}
KJV: [phrase] owl.

H3285.definition:
from the same as H3283 (יָעֵן); responsive;
Jaanai, an Israelite
KJV: Jaanai.

H3286.definition:
a primitive root;
to tire (as if from wearisome flight)
KJV: faint, cause to fly, (be) weary (self).

H3287.definition:
from H3286 (יָעַף);
fatigued; figuratively, exhausted
KJV: faint, weary.

H3288.definition:
from H3286 (יָעַף);
fatigue (adverb, utterly exhausted)
KJV: swiftly.e

H3289.definition:
a primitive root;
to advise; reflexively, to deliberate or resolve
KJV: advertise, take advise, advise (well), consult, (give, take) counsel(-lor), determine, devise, guide, purpose.

H3290.definition:
from H6117 (עָקַב); heel-catcher (i.e. supplanter);
Jaakob, the Israelitish patriarch
KJV: Jacob.

H3291.definition:
from H3290 (יַעֲקֹב);
Jaakobah, an Israelite
KJV: Jaakobah.

H3292.definition:
from the same as H6130 (עָקָן);
Jaakan, an Idumaean
KJV: Jaakan. Compare H1142 (בְּנֵי יַעֲקָן).

H3293.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to thicken with verdure;
a copse of bushes; hence, a forest; hence, honey in the comb (as hived in trees)
KJV: (honey-) comb, forest, wood.

H3294.definition:
a form of H3295 (יַעֲרָה);
Jarah, an Israelite
KJV: Jarah.

H3295.definition:
feminine of H3293 (יַעַר), and meaning the same
{a copse of bushes; hence, a forest; hence, honey in the comb (as hived in trees)}
KJV: (honey-) comb, forest.

H3296.definition:
from the plural of H3293 (יַעַר) and the masculine plural active participle of H707 (אָרַג); woods of weavers;
Jaare-Oregim, an Israelite
KJV: Jaare-oregim.

H3297.definition:
plural of H3293 (יַעַר); forests;
Jearim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Jearim. Compare H7157 (קִרְיַת יְעָרִים).

H3298.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain signification and H3050 (יָהּ);
Jaareshjah, an Israelite
KJV: Jaresiah.

H3299.definition:
from H6213 (עָשָׂה); they will do;
Jaasu, an Israelite
KJV: Jaasau.
